## Something needs root
```
{{PROJECT_NAME}} needs root for: [what — e.g. installing a package, a udev
rule, mounting an image, binding port 80].
Put it in tools/setup.sh: short, idempotent, commented, root-only work.
Then tell me the one-line summary I should send the owner for approval.
```
Sessions have no general sudo. the owner approves the script by hash from Discord
(`/sudo action:approve project:{{PROJECT_NAME}} script:tools/setup.sh`), after
which `sudo tools/setup.sh` works — and `sudo` commands *inside* it are
allowed. Editing the file cancels the approval. Only if the long-running
process itself must be root does `launch.sh` get `SUDO=sudo` and its own
approval.

